From: Armada <noreply@armada>
Subject: [PATCH] msm_dpu metrics: fdinfo memory, gpu thermal names, honest cpu power

The preset Steam enables on ARM handhelds (preset 2) asks for vram,
gpu_core_clock and cpu_power. On this board all three read as 0:

 - gpu_fdinfo never picked a memory key for msm_dpu, even though the msm
   driver writes drm-total-memory / drm-resident-memory into every client's
   fdinfo, and the vram element reads sys_vram_used (device-wide), which no
   msm sysfs ever fills. Adreno has no dedicated VRAM, so the resident GEM
   bytes are the honest device-wide number.
 - msm_metrics::Temperatures matched gpuss_N_N_thermal / gpu_thermal / gpu,
   but thermal-hwmon names zones after the DT node: this tree registers
   gpu_top_thermal and gpu_bottom_thermal, so regex_match found nothing.
 - memory temp only accepted spd5118 / ddr_thermal; the DT zone here is
   mem_thermal.
 - cpu_power printed GetCPUDataTotal().power unconditionally. There is no
   k10temp/zenpower/zenergy/rapl/amdgpu/xgene sensor on SM8450, so the row
   showed a fabricated 0 W next to a real battery wattage.

diff --git a/src/cpu.h b/src/cpu.h
--- a/src/cpu.h
+++ b/src/cpu.h
@@ -192,6 +192,11 @@ public:
    const CPUData& GetCPUDataTotal() const {
       return m_cpuDataTotal;
    }
+   // No ARM SoC here exposes a package power sensor, so InitCpuPowerData leaves
+   // the power source null; without this the overlay draws a silent 0 W.
+   bool hasCpuPower() const {
+      return m_cpuPowerData != nullptr;
+   }
 private:
    unsigned long long int m_boottime = 0;
    std::vector<CPUData> m_cpuData;
diff --git a/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp b/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
--- a/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
+++ b/src/gpu_fdinfo.cpp
@@ -794,6 +794,11 @@ void GPU_fdinfo::main_thread()
         metrics.load = get_gpu_load();
         metrics.proc_vram_used = get_memory_used();
 
+        if (module == "msm_dpu")
+            // Adreno has no dedicated VRAM: the resident GEM bytes are the only
+            // device-wide memory accounting the msm driver publishes.
+            metrics.sys_vram_used = metrics.proc_vram_used;
+
         metrics.powerUsage = get_power_usage();
         metrics.powerLimit = static_cast<float>(hwmon_sensors["power_limit"].val) / 1'000'000;
 
diff --git a/src/gpu_fdinfo.h b/src/gpu_fdinfo.h
--- a/src/gpu_fdinfo.h
+++ b/src/gpu_fdinfo.h
@@ -151,8 +151,10 @@ public:
             drm_engine_type = "drm-engine-gfx";
             drm_memory_type = "drm-memory-vram";
         } else if (module == "msm_dpu") {
-            // msm driver does not report vram usage
+            // msm has no kgsl-style sysfs, but it does report per-client GEM
+            // accounting in fdinfo: drm-total-memory / drm-resident-memory.
             drm_engine_type = "drm-engine-gpu";
+            drm_memory_type = "drm-resident-memory";
             init_kgsl();
         } else if (module == "msm_drm") {
             init_kgsl();
